# Palanca-OT colouring rules (Module 4). First matching rule wins, so OT rules come first.
@OT: ARP spoofing (duplicate IP)@arp.duplicate-address-detected || arp.duplicate-address-frame@[45000,0,0][65535,65535,65535]
@OT: Modbus WRITE (FC 05/06/15/16)@modbus.func_code in {5,6,15,16}@[52000,0,52000][65535,65535,65535]
@OT: Modbus EXCEPTION reply@modbus.exception_code@[65535,42000,0][0,0,0]
@OT: Modbus diagnostics / device ID (FC 08/17/43)@modbus.func_code in {8,17,43}@[40000,30000,65535][0,0,0]
@OT: PLC programming port (S7 / TCP 102)@tcp.port == 102@[65535,55000,0][0,0,0]
@OT: New connection attempt (SYN, no ACK)@tcp.flags.syn == 1 && tcp.flags.ack == 0@[65535,65535,30000][0,0,0]
@OT: Modbus read (FC 01-04)@modbus.func_code in {1,2,3,4}@[52000,65535,52000][0,0,0]
@OT: OPC UA@opcua@[45000,55000,65535][0,0,0]
@OT: SNMP@snmp@[58000,58000,58000][0,0,0]
